@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# Jaeger implementation progress
+
+Owner-requested durable checkpoint, 2026-11-18. Update this file from evidence;
+do not convert activity into a completion percentage. Deployment requires
+separate permission. The Mac Studio runtime is not the development workspace.
+
+## Working now — development candidate
+
+The Gateway preserves a classified provider failure in the terminal request
+receipt and SSE event. Exhausted credits become `needs_owner`; the existing
+durable task owner stops retrying, retains the original error and actionable
+diagnosis, and delivers the outcome once. A fresh owner does not restart it.
+Transient failures retain their bounded retry. Cancellation and unknown effects
+retain precedence over a provider diagnosis.
+
+The shared chat UI uses the same Gateway diagnosis for live errors and restored
+history, keeping the raw error under Details. No UI redesign or alternate
+execution path was introduced.
+
+The existing task owner passed a process-level recovery check: a controlled
+worker executed real candidate regression tests, committed the result to
+SQLite, and exited before settling the task. Two subsequent owner processes
+recovered one verified artifact and one delivery, with exactly one worker
+execution. This verifies task persistence/reconciliation with a deterministic
+test worker; it is **not** evidence of autonomous model-written fixes.
+
+## Changes made
+
+- Reuse `jaeger_agent.core.errors` at the Gateway's failure producer.
+- Honor explicit owner blockers when settling failed task cards; retain unknown
+  effect and cancellation protections.
+- Carry the human diagnosis through SSE, durable request recovery, and chat rendering.
+- Add regression and subprocess recovery coverage. Retain the existing Gateway,
+  task owner, store, scheduler, permissions, and model-routing architecture.
+- Record the owner's new production/development boundary in `AGENTS.md`.
+
+## Validation and artifacts
+
+Base: `e00600741ed11ebb0d05480f1f51eecb4eb528d9`.
+Candidate branch: `codex/autonomy-baseline`.
+Candidate commit: the commit introducing this checkpoint (`git log -1 -- docs/PROGRESS.md`).
+
+Development used an independent clone, disposable HOME/state/cache, copied UI
+dependencies, and a macOS sandbox. Explicit probes confirmed that the test
+process cannot read/write the production checkout or connect to Gateway 33418.
+Only the candidate's code was imported. No production credentials were copied.
+The installed Python dependencies were read-only; the UI build stayed external.
+
+Evidence directory beside the retained candidate: `evidence/`.
+
+- `quota-before.log`: both new regression tests failed on the original code;
+  the durable credit-blocked task incorrectly returned to `queued`.
+- `backend-final.log`: **58 passed**, including provider/task/terminal/recovery checks.
+  Two HTTP tests are explicitly excluded because their random listener ports
+  are denied by the isolation profile; they are not claimed as passing.
+- `ui-focused.log`: TypeScript passed; 30 UI checks passed, including all three
+  new diagnosis tests. One existing stop-progress expectation failed.
+- `ui-baseline.log`: that same stop-progress test fails on unchanged base source.
+- `ui-build.log`: canonical frontend production build and no-mock check passed.
+- `verify-all.log`: required `scripts/verify.sh` ran; hygiene passed, then IDE
+  tests stopped the pipeline with three sandbox-denied listener failures
+  (`EPERM`). The full pipeline is not green.
+
+No production deployment, restart, installed-app update, remote push, or provider
+switch was performed during this implementation session. The live bridge's
+read-only health query returned ready; that is not proof of inference.
+
+## Milestone status and blockers
+
+1. **Reliable chat/agent baseline: incomplete.** The prior live Grok smoke test
+   returned HTTP 402 (credits/subscription). This candidate diagnoses that failure;
+   it does not fund an account or establish a working development inference route.
+2. **Durable bounded background work: component proof obtained.** Process recovery,
+   verification artifacts, no duplicate execution, and one delivery pass with a
+   controlled worker. Full model/tool execution across a service restart remains
+   unqualified in an approved development deployment.
+3. **Research → candidate code → independent test → retained result: incomplete.**
+   Codex made this candidate; Jaeger has not yet autonomously authored it.
+4. Self-development, video drafts, and continuous multi-workflow operation remain
+   unqualified. No unattended daily job was enabled on production.
+
+## Next task
+
+Establish a successful isolated development chat/tool turn using an available,
+authorized provider, persist the receipt, and then run one bounded defect-fix
+objective through the existing durable task owner in an isolated Git branch.
+Keep the evaluator and deployment approval outside the worker's edit authority.
+Do not expand research or content automation before this works.
